From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nuno407 <11352538+nuno407@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:13:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 42/45] ASoC: wm8962: resume the codec to set up microphone
 detection

wm8962_mic_detect() updates ADDITIONAL_CONTROL_4, a volatile register.
Called from the machine driver while the codec is runtime suspended
(regcache cache only), the update failed and MICDET_ENA was never set,
on some boots of the Surface RT:

  wm8962 4-001a: ASoC error (-16): at snd_soc_component_update_bits()
  on wm8962.4-001a for register: [0x00000030]

Take a runtime PM reference around the register updates.
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wm8962.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wm8962.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wm8962.c
index 8ed1f4aac..c173a2e53 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wm8962.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wm8962.c
@@ -3240,7 +3240,7 @@ int wm8962_mic_detect(struct snd_soc_component *component, struct snd_soc_jack *
 {
 	struct wm8962_priv *wm8962 = snd_soc_component_get_drvdata(component);
 	struct snd_soc_dapm_context *dapm = snd_soc_component_to_dapm(component);
-	int irq_mask, enable;
+	int irq_mask, enable, ret;
 
 	wm8962->jack = jack;
 	if (jack) {
@@ -3251,11 +3251,22 @@ int wm8962_mic_detect(struct snd_soc_component *component, struct snd_soc_jack *
 		enable = 0;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * ADDITIONAL_CONTROL_4 is volatile: while the codec is runtime
+	 * suspended (cache only) the update fails with -EBUSY and the
+	 * detection is never enabled. Resume it for the writes.
+	 */
+	ret = pm_runtime_resume_and_get(component->dev);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
+
 	snd_soc_component_update_bits(component, WM8962_INTERRUPT_STATUS_2_MASK,
 			    WM8962_MICD_EINT | WM8962_MICSCD_EINT, irq_mask);
 	snd_soc_component_update_bits(component, WM8962_ADDITIONAL_CONTROL_4,
 			    WM8962_MICDET_ENA, enable);
 
+	pm_runtime_put(component->dev);
+
 	/* Send an initial empty report */
 	snd_soc_jack_report(wm8962->jack, 0,
 			    SND_JACK_MICROPHONE | SND_JACK_BTN_0);
-- 
